# 🔥🔥🔥 Pattern Recognition Cheat Sheet

```text
Chunk array
→ slice() + jump by size

Rotate array
→ cut + join in different order

Move zeros
→ keep non-zero values first

Pair sum
→ target - current

Sort objects
→ sort() + comparator

Group objects
→ reduce() + dynamic keys
```

---

# 🧠 VERY IMPORTANT INTERVIEW PATTERNS

### Pattern 1 — Dynamic object key

You will see:

```js
groups[key];
```

This means:

> Use the value stored in `key` as the object property.

Example:

```js
const key = "IT";

groups[key];
```

means:

```js
groups.IT;
```

---

### Pattern 2 — `target - current`

For pair-sum problems:

```js
const needed = target - num;
```

If:

```text
target = 10
num = 6
```

then:

```text
needed = 4
```

So we ask:

> Have I already seen `4`?

---

### Pattern 3 — `reduce()` to group

Remember:

```js
array.reduce((result, item) => {
  const key = item.property;

  if (!result[key]) {
    result[key] = [];
  }

  result[key].push(item);

  return result;
}, {});
```

This pattern appears constantly in real JavaScript work.

